Lab 8: Create Groups and Assign Permissions
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Create and manage user groups in Linux systems
Understand the principle of least privilege in access control
Assign appropriate permissions to different user groups based on their roles
Configure group-based access control for files and directories
Test and verify user access permissions
Implement role-based security models using Linux groups
Troubleshoot common permission-related issues
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line interface
Knowledge of file and directory permissions (rwx)
Familiarity with user management concepts
Understanding of sudo privileges
Basic knowledge of text editors (nano, vim, or vi)
Completed previous labs on user management
