Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: Permission Denied Errors
If users cannot access directories they should have access to:

# Check file ownership and permissions
ls -la /opt/company_project/
ls -la /opt/company_project/*/

# Verify group memberships
id username
groups username

# Check ACLs if configured
getfacl /path/to/directory
Issue 2: Sudo Access Problems
If sudo commands are not working:

# Verify sudoers files
sudo visudo -c
sudo visudo -c -f /etc/sudoers.d/admins
sudo visudo -c -f /etc/sudoers.d/developers

# Check sudoers file syntax
sudo cat /etc/sudoers.d/admins
Issue 3: Group Assignment Issues
If users are not properly assigned to groups:

# Re-add user to group
sudo usermod -a -G groupname username

# Force group refresh (user may need to log out/in)
newgrp groupname
Security Best Practices Implemented
Principle of Least Privilege
Admins: Full system access only when necessary
Developers: Limited to development tools and specific services
Viewers: Read-only access to public documentation
Defense in Depth
Multiple permission layers (file permissions, ACLs, sudoers)
Group-based access control
Directory-level restrictions
Audit Trail
All sudo commands are logged
File access can be monitored
Group membership changes are tracked
